+/*
+ * NABU (Xiaomi Pad 5, SM8150) touch: Novatek NT36523 on GENI SPI SE19.
+ *
+ * Separate from sweet_touch.c (Goodix/FTS *I2C* on SE7): nabu's panel is a
+ * Novatek NT36523 on QUPv3 wrapper-2 SE1 (= "qup18", SPI) at 0x00c84000.
+ * Enabled by boot-arg nabutouch=1 (default off); on nabu also pass
+ * sweettouch=0 so the SE7 I2C probe does not run.
+ *
+ * Written blind for CI bring-up. ABL leaves SE19 running the *I2C* GENI
+ * firmware (proto=3), so before any SPI we load the GENI *SPI* serial-engine
+ * firmware into the SE's config RAM, exactly as the downstream kernel does
+ * (sequence from the mainline "load QUP SE Firmware" patch; the SPI SEFW
+ * image is lifted from the device's own qupfw partition, two QUPV3 core
+ * versions, selected at runtime by QUP_HW_VER). Only then does proto become
+ * SPI and the FIFO engine work.
+ *
+ * It does NOT reset the NT36523 or download its controller firmware; it
+ * assumes that stays resident across the fastboot handoff. First it confirms
+ * SPI comms (FWINFO at EVENT_BUF+0x78), then polls the event buffer.
+ *
+ * Register facts (Linux v6.6 + MiCode nabu + the SE-FW-load patch):
+ *   gcc-sm8150.c:   wrap2_s2 RCG 0x1e3a8; branch vote 0x52014 (s2 BIT6,
+ *                   m-ahb BIT2, s-ahb BIT1).
+ *   pinctrl-sm8150: gpio55-58 SOUTH tile (0x03d00000), ctl pin*0x1000, qup19
+ *                   = mux 2; mux_bit 2, pull_bit 0, drv_bit 6, oe 9.
+ *   geniqup@cc0000: wrapper-2; QUP_HW_VER at +0x4.
+ *   SE FW load:     CGC 0x28, CLK_CTRL 0x2000, CFG_REG0 0x100, CFG_RAMN
+ *                   0x1010, FW_REVISION 0x1000/0x1004, INIT_CFG 0x0/0x4,
+ *                   DMA_IF_EN 0x2004, FIFO_IF_DISABLE 0x2008, PROG_RAM
+ *                   SCLK/HCLK off BIT9/BIT8, DMA_GENERAL_CFG 0xe30.
+ *   MiCode nt36523: EVENT_BUF_ADDR 0x2FE00, read=clear bit7, 1 dummy byte.
+ */
